# Hardware Architecture & System Setup

## Physical System Setup
Below is the prototype implementation showing the ESP32 microcontroller, integrated sensor suite, power supply, LCD readout, and motor actuator.

![Hardware Setup](../images/hardware_setup.jpg)

---

## Bill of Materials (BOM)
* **Microcontroller:** ESP32 Development Board
* **Soil Moisture Sensor:** Resistive/Capacitive Soil Moisture Sensor Module
* **Temperature Sensor:** DS18B20 Waterproof Stainless Steel Probe
* **Humidity Sensor:** DHT11 Sensor Module
* **Display:** 16x2 I2C LCD Display
* **Actuator:** 5V Single-Channel Relay Module with 3-6V Mini Submersible Water Pump
* **Power Supply:** 3x 18650 Lithium-ion Battery Holder Pack

---

## Pin Connection Mapping

| Component | Module Pin | ESP32 GPIO Pin | Function |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Soil Moisture** | AO (Analog Out) | GPIO 34 | Soil moisture level detection (ADC) |
| **DS18B20 Probe** | Data | GPIO 4 | Soil/Ambient temperature reading (OneWire) |
| **DHT11 Sensor** | Data | GPIO 5 | Humidity measurement |
| **Relay Module** | IN (Control) | GPIO 18 | Triggers water pump (HIGH = ON, LOW = OFF) |
| **I2C LCD Display**| SDA | GPIO 21 | Serial Data Line |
| **I2C LCD Display**| SCL | GPIO 22 | Serial Clock Line |
